.TH THINKPAD\-SETTINGS 1 "2026-07-26" "thinkpad-settings 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thinkpad\-settings \- edit ThinkPad firmware settings from the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thinkpad\-settings
.RI [ GTK\ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thinkpad\-settings
is a graphical editor for the firmware (BIOS/UEFI) settings that a Lenovo
ThinkPad exposes to Linux through the
.B think_lmi
kernel driver.
.PP
Settings are grouped into readable categories, each with a plain-English
description of what the setting actually does under Linux. Changes are
.I staged
locally and written together when you press Apply, so you are asked to
authenticate once no matter how many settings you edit.
.PP
The program runs unprivileged. All reads and writes go through
.BR fwupd (8)
on the system bus, and privilege is obtained through polkit, so nothing is
setuid and neither
.BR sudo (8)
nor
.BR pkexec (1)
is invoked.
.SH OPTIONS
The program takes no options of its own. Standard GTK options such as
.B \-\-display
are accepted.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Two polkit actions are involved:
.TP
.B org.freedesktop.fwupd.get\-bios\-settings
Required to read values. Configured as
.I auth_admin_keep
by default, so you are asked once per session.
.TP
.B org.freedesktop.fwupd.set\-bios\-settings
Required to write. Configured as
.IR auth_admin ,
so it prompts on every Apply.
.PP
If authentication is declined, fwupd returns the settings list with every
value withheld rather than reporting an error. The program detects this and
asks you to authenticate instead of displaying values it does not have.
.SH CAVEATS
.TP
.B Most settings need a restart
Firmware applies them during startup. A banner appears while changes are
staged but not yet active.
.TP
.B fwupd caches settings at daemon startup
If a setting is changed outside this program \(em in BIOS setup, or by writing
to sysfs directly \(em fwupd keeps reporting the previous value until it is
restarted. Run
.B systemctl restart fwupd
and then refresh.
.TP
.B The boot order cannot be changed here
fwupd validates a written value against the attribute's list of permitted
values.
.B BootOrder
holds a colon-separated sequence while its permitted values are single device
codes, so every reordering is rejected. The current order is shown read-only;
change it in BIOS setup by pressing F1 during startup.
.TP
.B Some settings are irreversible
Values named
.I PermanentlyDisable
cannot be undone on the affected machine. These are marked in the interface and
require confirmation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/firmware\-attributes/thinklmi/attributes/
The kernel interface the settings ultimately come from. Read by fwupd, not by
this program directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on normal exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fwupdmgr (1),
.BR fwupd (8),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
The same settings can be inspected from a terminal with
.BR "fwupdmgr get-bios-settings" .
.SH BUGS
Requires a machine whose firmware exposes settings through
.BR think_lmi .
Other vendors' firmware\-attributes drivers are untested.
